ch task under the tasks section, using the correct YAML syntax. I'll ensure there are no extra comments or explanations, just the tasks as specified.\n\nI should also check that the YAML is valid. Maybe I can run it through a linter to catch any issues, but since I'm writing it manually, I'll be careful with the indentation and colons.\n\nSo, the final playbook will start with '---', then a list of tasks, each with their respective modules and parameters. Each task will have a name and the appropriate module arguments.\n\nI think that covers all the requirements. Now, I'll write out the playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  local_action: \n    module: assert\n\n- name: Install vsftpd\n  apt:\n    name: vsftpd\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure vsftpd\n  template:\n    src: vsftpd.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/vsftpd.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: restart vsftpd\n\n- name: Start and enable vsftpd\n  service:\n    name: vsftpd\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-04T12:25:46.545317427Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14530646860, 'load_duration': 73461883, 'prompt_eval_count': 451, 'prompt_eval_duration': 132221645, 'eval_count': 710, 'eval_duration': 14323665899, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--da814bdd-a46f-46ae-a2a3-6c1d5e38e80e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 451, 'output_tokens': 710, 'total_tokens': 1161}
