eady. Using wait_for_port with the port 8200 and a timeout of 60 seconds ensures the service is up before proceeding.\n\nLastly, the sixth task retrieves Vault's initial root token. It uses command to execute the vault operator init command, captures the output, and registers it to a variable for later use.\n\nI need to make sure all these tasks are correctly ordered and that each module is called with the right parameters. I'll avoid adding any comments or explanations as per the user's instructions. The output should be a YAML file with the tasks in the exact order provided, no extra lines, and starting with '---'.\n\nI should also check for any possible YAML syntax errors, ensuring that all keys have proper colons and that the indentation is consistent. Since the playbook is meant to be included in a role, I don't need to worry about other role structures, just the tasks.\n\nIn summary, I'll structure the playbook starting with '---', then include each task in the specified order, using the correct modules and arguments. I'll ensure YAML validity and proper formatting without any additional comments or text beyond the playbook itself.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Copy Vault certificate\n  copy:\n    remote_src: no\n    src: /path/to/VAULT_CRT\n    dest: /etc/vault.d/vault.crt\n    remote_user: vault\n\n- name: Install Vault package\n  apt:\n    name: vault\n    state: present\n    update_cache: yes\n\n- name: Configure Vault server settings\n  template:\n    src: vault.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/vault.d/vault.conf\n    dir_mode: 755\n    mode: 644\n\n- name: Start Vault service\n  service:\n    name: vault\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n- name: Wait for Vault to be ready\n  wait_for_port:\n    host: 127.0.0.1\n    port: 8200\n    timeout: 60\n\n- name: Get Vault initial root token\n  command: vault operator init -init-root-token\n  register: vault_root_token\n  changed_when: false\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14