ks are in the correct order and that variables and modules are used accurately. I\'ll also ensure that each task is correctly indented and follows YAML syntax to pass yamllint and ansible-lint.\n\nLet me double-check each task to ensure I haven\'t missed any conditions or variables. Once everything is in place, I\'ll structure the playbook accordingly, making sure it\'s valid within an Ansible Role under the tasks directory.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  remote_host: localhost\n\n- name: Install apache httpd\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  when: selinux_enabled\n  setsebool:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: on\n  with_items: "{{ httpd_sebooleans }}"\n  notify: httpd_config_test\n\n- name: Configure httpd\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_config_src }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_dest }}"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: \n    - httpd_config_test\n    - httpd_service_restart\n\n- name: Activate httpd module | Debian\n  when: ansible_os_family == \'Debian\'\n  command: a2enmod\n  args:\n    modules: "{{ item }}"\n  with_items: "{{ httpd_modules_to_activate_with_command }}"\n\n- name: Import ssl.yml\n  import_tasks: ssl.yml\n  when: https_ssl_enable\n\n- name: Import locations.yml\n  import_tasks: locations.yml\n  when: httpd_locations is defined\n\n- name: Import vhosts.yml\n  import_tasks: vhosts.yml\n  when: httpd_vhosts is defined\n\n- name: Configure ports\n  when: ansible_os_family in [\'Debian\', \'Suse\']\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_ports_config_src }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_ports_config_dest }}"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: \n    - httpd_config_test\n    - httpd_service_restart\n\n- name: Import directories.yml\n  import_tasks: directories.yml\n  when: httpd_directories is defined\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Removing default html\n  when: httpd_remove_example\n  file:\n    path: "{{ httpd_data_directory }}/example.