re. I\'ll avoid adding any comments or extra lines, just the tasks as specified. Each module should be correctly formatted, and variables should be properly referenced with double curly braces.\n\nI should also check if each task has the necessary parameters and if the order is correct. No tasks should be omitted or modified, and the entire playbook should be valid YAML that can be included in an Ansible Role under tasks/main.yml.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all the points. Now, I\'ll structure the playbook step by step, making sure each task is correctly implemented as per the instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assertion file\n  assert:\n    file: assert.yml\n    run_once: true\n  remote_host: localhost\n\n- name: Enable Redis module stream for RHEL 8\n  dnf:\n    name: ".redis-module-redislabs"\n    state: present\n    repoquery:\n      list: installed\n      name: ".redis-module-redislabs"\n\n- name: Install Redis package\n  package:\n    name: "{{ redis_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure Redis settings\n  template:\n    src: redis.conf-{{ ansible_distribution }}.j2\n    dest: /etc/redis.conf\n    owner: "{{ redis_owner }}"\n    group: "{{ redis_group }}"\n    mode: "{{ redis_mode }}"\n  notify: restart_redis\n\n- name: Start and enable Redis service\n  service:\n    name: "{{ redis_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-04T14:08:53.597651265Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12679268037, 'load_duration': 90952547, 'prompt_eval_count': 421, 'prompt_eval_duration': 99380770, 'eval_count': 726, 'eval_duration': 12487450822, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--a6a872d3-3786-474f-8bf0-4cbc299ade1e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 421, 'output_tokens': 726, 'total_tokens': 1147}
