content='<think>\nAlright, let\'s tackle this problem. I need to correct the Ansible playbook so that it passes ansible-lint without changing the functional intent. The original playbook had several issues, mainly related to using non-FQCN module names and some linting errors about parameters and modes.\n\nFirst, I\'ll look at the errors. The main issues are:\n\n1. Non-FQCN module names: The modules like openssl_privatekey, openssl_csr, etc., are being used without their full namespace. Ansible expects FQCN (Fully Qualified Class Names) for modules, which typically include the collection name. In this case, the community.crypto collection is likely the right place, so I\'ll prefix each module with community.crypto.\n\n2. Unsupported parameters: The openssl_privatekey module was given a \'provider\' parameter, which might not be supported. I\'ll check the documentation to see if \'provider\' is valid. It seems that for RSA, the \'type\' parameter is used instead, so I\'ll replace \'provider\' with \'type\' and set it to \'rsa\'.\n\n3. Missing parameters: The openssl_certificate task was missing the \'provider\' parameter, which is required. I\'ll add \'provider: selfsigned\' since we\'re creating a self-signed certificate.\n\n4. Module arguments: The file module was using \'content\' incorrectly. Instead, I should use \'src\' to specify the file to read. Also, the \'combine\' module was used, which is deprecated. I\'ll replace it with a shell command that concatenates the files directly.\n\n5. Mode settings: The \'mode\' parameter was given as 600, which is an integer. Ansible expects it to be a string, so I\'ll change it to "600". Alternatively, using symbolic mode like \'0o600\' would also be correct, but "600" is more straightforward.\n\n6. Correcting tasks: I\'ll ensure all tasks use the correct FQCN and that parameters are supported. For example, the openssl_pkcs12 module was missing the \'certificate_path\' and \'privatekey_path\' parameters, so I\'ll add those.\n\n7. Variable handling: The file module was incorrectly trying to set \'content\' as a variable. Instead, I\'ll use \'register\' correctly and ensure that the content is read properly.\n\nBy addressing each of these points step by step, I can correct the playbook to pass ansible-lint while keeping the tasks as intended.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Generate an OpenSSL private key\n  community.crypto.openssl_privatekey:\n    path: /etc/ssl/private/private.key\n    type: rsa\n    size: 4096\n    mode: "600"\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Generate an OpenSSL Certificate Signing Request (CSR)\n  community.crypto.openssl_csr:\n    path: /etc/ssl/csr/csr.pem\n    privatekey_path: /etc/ssl/private/private.key\n    subject:\n      common_name: example.com\n    mode: "600"\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Generate an OpenSSL X.509 certificate\n  community.crypto.x509_certificate:\n    path: /etc/ssl/certs/cert.pem\n    privatekey_path: /etc/ssl/private/private.key\n    csr_path: /etc/ssl/csr/csr.pem\n    validity: 365\n    provider: selfsigned\n    mode: "600"\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Generate a PKCS#12 file\n  community.crypto.openssl_pkcs12:\n    name: /etc/ssl/keycert.p12\n    privatekey_path: /etc/ssl/private/private.key\n    certificate_path: /etc/ssl/certs/cert.pem\n    password: changeit\n    mode: "600"\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Read private key content\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/ssl/private/private.key\n    state: file\n  register: private_key_content\n\n- name: Read certificate content\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/ssl/certs/cert.pem\n    state: file\n  register: certificate_content\n\n- name: Create a combined private key and certificate file\n  shell: cat /etc/ssl/private/private.key /etc/ssl/certs/cert.pem > /etc/ssl/keycert.pem\n  args:\n    chdir: /etc/ssl\n  register: keycert_content\n\n- name: Write combined key and certificate to file\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/ssl/keycert.pem\n    content: "{{ keycert_content.stdout }}"\n    mode: "600"\n    owner: root\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-04T14:10:55.509835407Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 26043489832, 'load_duration': 84283684, 'prompt_eval_count': 4316, 'prompt_eval_duration': 2860645950, 'eval_count': 993, 'eval_duration': 23097788308, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--50dd9521-0149-46b8-959d-82dc3ecda35f-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4316, 'output_tokens': 993, 'total_tokens': 5309}
