r vars sections since the playbook is meant to be part of a role, not a standalone playbook. I also ensured the YAML structure was correct, starting with '---' and proper indentation.\n\nThroughout the process, I kept in mind the need for strict adherence to the given instructions, avoiding any extra elements or deviations. This approach should result in a valid and functional Ansible Playbook that meets all specified requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n    host: localhost\n\n- name: Install nginx\n  apt:\n    name: nginx\n    state: present\n\n- name: Place nginx.conf\n  template:\n    src: nginx.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: restart_nginx\n\n- name: Ensure /etc/nginx/conf.d exists\n  file:\n    path: /etc/nginx/conf.d\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n  notify: restart_nginx\n\n- name: Place default.conf\n  template:\n    src: default.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: restart_nginx\n\n- name: Start and enable nginx\n  systemd:\n    name: nginx\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-04T15:37:05.602291989Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12841716593, 'load_duration': 85493408, 'prompt_eval_count': 420, 'prompt_eval_duration': 105890432, 'eval_count': 736, 'eval_duration': 12649618476, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--82696509-d36e-4055-a205-8e142c3a9123-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 420, 'output_tokens': 736, 'total_tokens': 1156}
