ook will have three tasks in the specified order. Each task uses the appropriate module and parameters. I'll double-check each module's usage to ensure accuracy. For example, in Task 1, the repo key should be 'backports' and the state set to present. In Task 3, the name parameter for apt should be 'ansible' with the correct version from Backports.\n\nI should also consider if any of these tasks might fail on certain systems. For instance, if the system isn't Debian-based, Task 1 might not apply, but the user specified Debian-based, so it should be safe.\n\nFinally, I'll compile the YAML, ensuring it starts with '---' and each task follows correctly. I'll avoid any trailing spaces or formatting issues to pass yamllint and ansible-lint checks.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable Backports repository\n  apt:\n    repo: 'deb http://mirrors.debian.org/debian-backports/ {{ ansible_facts['debian_version'] }}-backports main'\n    state: present\n    update_cache: yes\n\n- name: Set the default_release option for older Debian versions\n  set_fact:\n    ansible_python_interpreter: /usr/bin/python3\n  when: ansible_distribution == 'debian' and ansible_debian_version is not defined\n\n- name: Install Ansible\n  apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n    version: '2.9'\n    repo: 'deb http://mirrors.debian.org/debian-backports/ {{ ansible_facts['debian_version'] }}-backports main'\n    update_cache: yes\n  register: install_result\n\n- name: Reboot if Ansible was installed\n  reboot:\n    reboot: yes\n    connect_timeout: 10\n    state: rebooted\n  when: install_result is not skipped and install_result.changed\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-04T15:38:19.68120969Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12885863708, 'load_duration': 92867044, 'prompt_eval_count': 338, 'prompt_eval_duration': 73231031, 'eval_count': 796, 'eval_duration': 12718839447, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='r